#. Versiones: 4.3.2, 5.0.2
msgctxt "books/To Emily.txt"
msgid ""
"My dearest Emily,\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Conditions in the mine have gotten so, so bad. It has been 2 weeks since I have been able to see your beautiful face, and the kids. Tomorrow, we are locking Baron Herx up in the bottom of the dungeons. I may never see the surface again. I may never see you again, which is my biggest regret. If I don’t, I have left 3,000 gold coins in the bedside drawer, and 10,000 goldsworth of stolen goods from the mine. \n"
"I worry that with the Baron trapped, the citizens of Hamlet will become complacent. Do not be tempted to stay. Move, Emily. Move far away from this wretched land. Escape through the sewers to avoid the women in the plaza if you must. Buy a house in the Hangats, and never look back. There is nothing but death and destruction left in Hamlet. \n"
"\n"
"I love you, Emily, never forget that. \n"
"\n"
"Always yours,\n"
"~Reggie"
msgstr ""
"Mi querida Emily:\n"
"\n"
"Las condiciones en la mina han empeorado tanto, tanto. Han pasado dos semanas desde que pude ver tu hermoso rostro y a los niños. Mañana encerraremos al Barón Herx en el fondo de las mazmorras. Quizá nunca vuelva a ver la superficie. Quizá nunca vuelva a verte, y eso es lo que más lamento. Si no regreso, he dejado 3.000 monedas de oro en el cajón junto a la cama y objetos robados de la mina por valor de otras 10.000.\n"
"Me preocupa que, una vez atrapado el Barón, los ciudadanos de Hamlet se confíen. No caigas en la tentación de quedarte. Márchate, Emily. Vete lejos de esta tierra miserable. Si hace falta, escapa por las alcantarillas para evitar a las mujeres de la plaza. Compra una casa en Hangats y nunca mires atrás. En Hamlet solo quedan muerte y destrucción.\n"
"\n"
"Te amo, Emily. Nunca lo olvides.\n"
"\n"
"Por siempre tuyo,\n"
"~Reggie\n"

